---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj28.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "The Balance Sheet Liability Method" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Deferred Tax Asset Recognition — the Recoverability Test" },
        { id: "s5", label: "THE KEY DIVERGENCE — the Company Classification (会社分類) Framework" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Measurement — Enacted or Substantively Enacted Tax Rates" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Applying the Company Classification Framework" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Measuring a Deferred Tax Liability at the Future Enacted Rate" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Recognising the future tax consequences of today's temporary differences</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 28 governs "TAX EFFECT ACCOUNTING" (税効果会計) — Japan's DEFERRED tax framework, addressing DIFFERENCES between an asset or liability's ACCOUNTING carrying amount and its TAX basis (temporary differences), recognising DEFERRED TAX assets and liabilities for the FUTURE tax consequences of those differences — broadly the SAME balance sheet liability method used under IAS 12 and ASC 740 internationally, though J-GAAP applies a genuinely DISTINCTIVE, STRUCTURED practical framework for assessing deferred tax ASSET recoverability (Section 5).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">All companies with temporary differences between accounting and tax bases</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies with TEMPORARY DIFFERENCES between the ACCOUNTING carrying amount of assets/liabilities and their TAX basis, requiring recognition of DEFERRED tax assets and liabilities for the resulting FUTURE tax effects.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Balance Sheet Liability Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Comparing carrying amounts to tax bases, item by item</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">DEFERRED tax is determined by COMPARING the ACCOUNTING carrying amount of EACH asset and liability to its TAX BASIS — TEMPORARY DIFFERENCES (e.g. a provision recognised for accounting purposes but not yet tax-deductible) give rise to a DEFERRED TAX ASSET or LIABILITY, reflecting the FUTURE tax consequence when the difference eventually REVERSES.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Deferred Tax Asset Recognition — the Recoverability Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Recognised only to the extent future taxable income is expected</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">A DEFERRED TAX ASSET is recognised ONLY to the EXTENT it is considered RECOVERABLE — that is, SUFFICIENT future TAXABLE income is expected to be available AGAINST WHICH the temporary difference (or tax loss carryforward) can be UTILISED. J-GAAP applies a genuinely STRUCTURED, PRESCRIPTIVE framework for making this assessment (Section 5), MORE FORMALISED than the general "probable" (IAS 12) or "more likely than not" (ASC 740) principles-based tests used internationally.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — the Company Classification (会社分類) Framework</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A tiered, structured system determining how much DTA can be recognised</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Under DETAILED implementation guidance supplementing this Statement, companies are CATEGORISED into a STRUCTURED "COMPANY CLASSIFICATION" (会社分類) system — GENERALLY numbered Classifications 1 through 5 — based on OBJECTIVE, HISTORICAL and PROJECTED profitability indicators (e.g. consistent recent TAXABLE income, existence of tax loss CARRYFORWARDS, or history of SIGNIFICANT losses). Each CLASSIFICATION carries SPECIFIC, PRESCRIBED rules for HOW MUCH of a deferred tax asset may be recognised (e.g. companies in the STRONGEST classification may recognise deferred tax assets FULLY, while companies in WEAKER classifications face INCREASINGLY restrictive limits, potentially permitting recognition ONLY for temporary differences expected to REVERSE within a limited future period, or NONE at all for the WEAKEST classification). This STRUCTURED, TIERED, RULE-BASED approach is a genuinely DISTINCTIVE J-GAAP feature — MORE PRESCRIPTIVE and FORMULA-DRIVEN than the MORE JUDGEMENT-BASED "probable"/"more likely than not" recoverability tests applied under IAS 12 and ASC 740, even though the UNDERLYING economic QUESTION (will future taxable income be sufficient?) is fundamentally the SAME.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Measurement — Enacted or Substantively Enacted Tax Rates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Using the rate expected to apply when the difference reverses</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">DEFERRED tax assets and liabilities are MEASURED using tax rates that are ENACTED (or SUBSTANTIVELY enacted) as of the reporting date, and EXPECTED to apply in the PERIOD the temporary difference is expected to REVERSE — broadly CONVERGED with both IAS 12 and ASC 740's measurement approach.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying the Company Classification Framework</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A structured, rule-based recoverability limit</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A company with a recent history of tax losses</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company has ¥200,000,000 of deferred tax assets arising from deductible temporary differences and tax loss carryforwards. Based on its recent history of losses and uncertain future profitability, it falls into a WEAKER company classification, limiting recognition to only the PORTION expected to reverse within the NEXT 5 years, estimated at ¥60,000,000.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a deferred tax asset of ONLY <strong>¥60,000,000</strong> — NOT the full ¥200,000,000 — with the REMAINING ¥140,000,000 UNRECOGNISED, reflecting the STRUCTURED classification-based recoverability LIMIT applicable to its specific circumstances.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Measuring a Deferred Tax Liability at the Future Enacted Rate</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Using the rate expected upon reversal, not today's rate</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A tax rate change already enacted</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company has a ¥50,000,000 taxable temporary difference expected to reverse in a future year when a NEWLY ENACTED lower tax rate of 28% (down from the current 30%) will apply.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The deferred tax LIABILITY is measured using the FUTURE, ALREADY-ENACTED 28% rate: ¥50,000,000 × 28% = <strong>¥14,000,000</strong> — NOT the CURRENT 30% rate — reflecting the rate EXPECTED to apply when the difference actually REVERSES.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 28 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Components and amounts of deferred tax assets and liabilities</span>
          <span>Reconciliation between the statutory tax rate and the effective tax rate</span>
          <span>Basis for assessing deferred tax asset recoverability, including company classification</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Determining the correct company classification for deferred tax asset recoverability purposes</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Projected future taxable income supporting the classification assessment</span>
              <span>Timing of reversal for temporary differences</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 12 and ASC 740</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-1-1-1">
            <span>Feature</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 28)</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IAS 12) / US GAAP (ASC 740)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-1-1"><span>Overall measurement approach</span><span>Balance sheet liability method</span><span>Balance sheet liability method — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-1-1"><span>DTA recoverability assessment</span><span>STRUCTURED company classification framework (Classifications 1–5)</span><span>General "probable" (IFRS) / "more likely than not" (US GAAP) judgement-based tests</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">The UNDERLYING deferred tax MECHANICS are broadly CONVERGED — the notable divergence is J-GAAP's MORE PRESCRIPTIVE, RULE-BASED recoverability framework, providing GREATER practical structure but LESS flexibility than the more judgement-driven international approaches.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every deferred tax event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Deferred tax asset/liability recognition</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Subject to the company classification recoverability framework</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 27</span><span>Current Income Taxes — supplies the current tax counterpart to this Statement's deferred tax treatment</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Company classification (会社分類)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A structured, tiered system (generally Classifications 1–5) categorising companies by profitability history, determining the extent to which deferred tax assets may be recognised.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Temporary difference</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A difference between the accounting carrying amount of an asset or liability and its tax basis, giving rise to a deferred tax asset or liability.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
        <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
        <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
        <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
        <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
